CM_ "MPC XY trajectory extension: dSPACE transmits 51 points in CAN IDs 515 through 565 (decimal) every 10 ms. Each frame contains IEEE-754 single-precision x and y in little-endian order. This schedule requires a 1 Mbit/s Classic CAN bus and careful total bus-load management. Transmit in ascending CAN-ID order; reception of ID 565 completes one trajectory set.";

CM_ BO_ 256 "Commit frame and watchdog input. IndustrialPC sends this frame after all active REF_POINT frames.";
CM_ SG_ 256 counter "Increment once per transmitted target set. Wraps at 65535.";
CM_ SG_ 256 state "Driving state: 0 lane, 1 waypoint, 2 avoid, 3 parking.";
CM_ SG_ 256 n_points "Number of valid REF_POINT frames in the current target set. Valid range 1 to 3.";
CM_ SG_ 256 v_ref "Final longitudinal target speed. Zero means stop; negative means reverse.";
CM_ SG_ 256 reserved "Reserved by protocol v2. Transmitter shall set zero.";

CM_ BO_ 257 "Reference point index 0 in the vehicle frame.";
CM_ BO_ 258 "Reference point index 1 in the vehicle frame.";
CM_ BO_ 259 "Reference point index 2 in the vehicle frame.";

CM_ BO_ 512 "Vehicle position feedback. First frame in the dSPACE feedback set.";
CM_ BO_ 513 "Vehicle yaw and velocity feedback. Second frame in the dSPACE feedback set.";
CM_ BO_ 514 "Vehicle steering feedback and commit counter. Send after VEH_POSE and VEH_VEL.";
CM_ SG_ 514 counter "Increment once per transmitted feedback set. Wraps at 65535.";
CM_ SG_ 514 reserved "Reserved by protocol v2. Transmitter shall set zero.";


